            <ArticleTitle>On the Horizon: The Synthetic Opioid U-49900.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1679</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7759/cureus.1679</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synthetic opioid use continues to be a problem in the United States. New designer opioids continue to be released as &quot;research chemicals&quot; by vendors, leading to widespread use and potentially devastating consequences. U-49900 is a new synthetic opioid with limited clinical data available. Herein, we provide an overview of U-49900, the anecdotal accounts of U-49900 use that clinicians need to be made aware of, and a call for the federal government to take immediate action in curtailing the use of U-49900.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
